                           Copyright 2025-2026 NXP


1) FOR MLANCSI APP ONLY BUILD

	Goto source code directory wlan_src/app/linux/mlancsi
	make [clean] build
	The app binaries can be found in mlancsi/ directory.

2) Supported Features
	- Configure filter(s) and start/stop flow of CSI from device to host
	- CSI processing for Ambient Motion index

3) Usage:
	The app in run as follows.
		- csi
			- Enable/disable channel state information collection

			- Usage :
				- mlancsi <interface> csi <disable/enable (config file)>
				Where:
					<interface> : mlan0 / uap0
					disable    	: 0
					enable     	: config file with csi filters

			- Example :
				- mlancsi mlan0 csi config/csi.conf       : Enable CSI
				- mlancsi mlan0 csi 0                     : Disable CSI

			Note: csi shall be enabled only after there is an active
				interface of uAP or STA connected to an ex-AP

		- Event monitoring mode to process CSI
			- The app monitors the events received from WLAN FW and filters for CSI events.
			- When a CSI event matches the CSI filter configured in mlancsi.conf

			- To Run the mlancsi driver app in event monitoring mode
			  Command Format :
				- mlancsi <interface> event <config_file>
				Where:
					<interface> : mlan0 / uap0
					<config_file> 	: Config file CSI event filter parameters
								: Default config file ( mlancsi.conf ) is present in config folder in release
					When no <config_file> is provided, CSI filter is set by first CSI event received and will run continously

				eg:
					./mlancsi mlan0 event config/mlancsi.conf - Capture the CSI event processing for mlan0 interface

4) Config file format for event monitoring mode
	i) Configure the MAC Source Address of CSI to be filtered (e.g., MAC address of AP)
		MAC_ADDR=02:50:43:24:C0:C1

	ii) Packet type and bandwidth
		For CSI records to be comparable they need to match in 802.11 PHY format and bandwidth
		Options
			Packet type:
				0: legacy - 11a/g
				1: HT         - 11n
				2: VHT        - 11ac
				3: HE         - 11ax
			PACKET_TYPE=3 (default value)

			Bandwidth:
				0: 20MHz
				1: 40MHz
				2: 80MHz
			FORMAT_BW=2

	iii) Algorithm configuration
		The ambient motion index calculates a change metric between the current CSI and a reference.
		There are multiple options to set and updated the reference
		Reference Update:
			0: "static"           - initialize with the first found CSI, no updates
			1: "IIR filter"       - initialize with the first found CSI, update with IIR fitler coefficient alpha
			2: "Kalman filter"	  -  initialize with the first found CSI, update with Kalaman fitler
		UPDATE_REF=0

		Parameters settings:
			IIR filter parameters
				IIR update filter H_ref_n = (1-alpha)*H_ref_{n-1) + alpha*H_n
				values within [0,1]
			IIR_ALPHA=0.1

			Kalman filter parameters
				Kalman filter update step:
				H_ref_n = (1-K_n)*H_ref_{n-1) + K_n*H_n
				where
				kp_0 = KALMAN_P0  // - initiatlization
				p_n = kp_{n-1} + KALMAN_ALPHA*delta_time
				S_n = p_n + KALMAN_N0
				K_n = p_n / S_n
				kp_n = (1 - K_n) * p_n
				delta_time in seconds
			KALMAN_P0=0.5
			KALMAN_ALPHA=0.005
			KALMAN_N0=0.2

		Number of CSI
			0:    default, will run until app is killed
			1-255:will run for this many CSI records
		NUM_CSI=0
5) When there is  requirement to dump the Event's raw data, following commands can be used.
       when it is required to dump event's raw data to screen only, use command:
       mlancsi <inerface> event dump_to_screen 1

       when it is required to dump event's raw data to file along with dump to screen.
       file name will be csidump_<interface_name>.txt, use command:
       mlancsi <inerface> event dump_to_file 1

       when it is required to dump event's raw data to screen along with processing, use command:
       mlancsi <interface> event config/<csi_filter_file_name> dump_to_screen

       when it is required to dump event's raw data to file(also to screen) along with processing.
       file name will be csidump_<interface_name>.txt, use command:
       mlancsi <interface> event config/<csi_filter_file_name> dump_to_file
